rain for example gpt  medium on python code for example using  that dgx station was really nice and i  really did need to use all four of those  uh a100 gpus so it is something that you  want to keep in mind the form factor of  the camino is also pretty impressive on  the right i have an air cooled box  machine with two rtx 8000s and on the  left i've got an air-cooled puget with  the two rtx 3090s  the kamino is basically the size of the  box just a little bit longer which makes  sense they're both rack mountable and  the puget is an atx xl size and it  honestly just looks like a giant next to  the camino but the kamino is more  powerful than the puget and the box put  together  also the dgx station was a atx xl size  so this tiny form factor for the 4x a100  build from kamino  really is impressive especially given  the temperatures that it runs at  so i think for me the trait that i find  most impressive here is just kamino's  ability to pack an abundance of  performance into  a relatively tiny form factor and the  reason that they can do this is because  of the water cooling and honestly being  willing to sort of rethink case design  and engineering because this casing  supports  all the way up to eatx motherboards as  big as they get  but it still has this pretty small form  factor it's such a unique build and at  least for me personally i  love the design i just love the way this  unit looks  very often we and i build computers and  slap on some rgb ram or fans or  something like that to make it look cool  but camino has just engineered cool here  there is just something about this  machine that i just love it  on the topic of cool i also recently  moved my operations to a far more uh and  better air conditioned area  so no longer am i breaking a sweat when  the machines are running  and the running temperatures of the  kamino under load are even better uh in  the 50s  again that's at full load  again i would love to see what the dgx  station runs in this same 